## Change

The response-header Java identity/API fixture previously covered 16 types,
while Rust defines 22. Added the six missing Java 5.5.1 types:
`AddWritePermOfBrokerResponseHeader`,
`ChangeInvisibleTimeResponseHeader`,
`GetAllSubscriptionGroupResponseHeader`,
`GetAllTopicConfigResponseHeader`, `GetKVConfigResponseHeader`, and
`WipeWritePermOfBrokerResponseHeader`. The Java class mapping records the
NameServer package and KV capitalization explicitly. Rust tests now require
22 identity and API inventory entries and verify the corresponding class
names and accessor mappings. No Rust production behavior changed.

Fixture SHA-256:
`4e17f64398e2ae742f1fae55841e365eb7aed89b3f6aaad7eb191e8d282dd8ae`.

